# ITSM Asistanı — Cursor rules

## Project
Repo: `nlu-insight-lab`. Product: **ITSM Asistanı**, an AI-supported ITSM chatbot (ticket classify, suggest, fill, report).

- UI, docs, user messages, taxonomy, bot replies, and ticket text are Turkish.
- Do not bring back marketplace returns, CFPB, or live ServiceNow APIs unless asked.

## Stack (do not change without asking)
Python 3.10+, Streamlit, scikit-learn, JSONL tickets.
No TypeScript, no extra web framework, no database unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture
Keep these layers separate; do not dump logic into `app.py`:

- `taxonomy.py` — Talep → Birim → Modül → Süreç (keyword, then `itsm_nlu.py`)
- `solutions.py` — past solution retrieval
- `slots.py` — field completion
- `sentiment.py` / `intents.py` / `rules.py` — signals
- `reports.py` — report command queue
- `orchestrator.py` — turn decision
- `tickets.py` / `summaries.py` — persistence and admin brief
- `auth.py` — local JSONL accounts
- `app.py` — UI only

The LLM (`llm_analyze.py`, Ollama) is optional and must not decide ticket vs self-serve. Default summaries are templates.

## Product rules
- Understand the request; clarify if the 4-level class is unclear.
- Offer matching ITSM solution records before opening a ticket (unless high-severity).
- Collect varlık / konum / etki, then open one ticket.
- Reporting commands are queued; `daily_jobs.py` is the JOB stand-in.
- Extra detail stays on the same ticket id.

## Coding
- Prefer small, readable Python. Type hints on new public functions.
- Do not add packages without asking.
- Before large refactors, check `PRD.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
